From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: d2d1: draw effects and command lists; fixes Paint.NET's UI needs

DrawImage of an effect drew nothing. Now the effect's transform graph is
drawn with Direct3D 11: each node renders into a 16-bit float texture over
the part of its output rectangle that is wanted. Draw transforms run their
own pixel shaders, with a vertex shader made to match the shader's inputs
(SV_POSITION, SCENE_POSITION, TEXCOORDn = input n's position and texel
size). Built-in effects use one internal shader with modes (premultiply,
unpremultiply, color matrix, sRGB/linear, opacity, flood, blur, resample,
shadow, invert). The result is drawn onto the target as a bitmap.

A command list can now be drawn: DrawImage plays it onto the context, under
the offset and clip the call asks for. As an effect's input it is first
played into a texture. Two command list bugs are fixed:
 - DrawGeometry was recorded without its geometry (NULL on replay, which
   crashed);
 - glyph runs, bitmap and image rectangles are kept after their command in
   a buffer that moves when it grows, so the recorded pointers dangled.
   They are now offsets from the command, resolved when streamed.

Geometries: ellipses, rounded rectangles and geometry groups simplify (to
lines or Béziers), so Widen and CombineWithGeometry work on them. Path
geometries stream into a geometry sink.

Also:
 - CreateBitmapFromWicBitmap takes 64bppPRGBA, 64bppPRGBAHalf,
   64bppRGBHalf, 128bppPRGBAFloat, 128bppRGBFloat and 8bppAlpha;
 - ID2D1Device::GetDxgiDevice, IsDxgiFormatSupported and IsSupported;
 - stroke styles are ID2D1StrokeStyle1;
 - the Crop effect has its BorderMode property, Composite its Mode, Shadow
   its three properties and 3DPerspectiveTransform its eight (two
   todo_wine in the tests now pass).

Gate: test/d2dfx-gate.sh.
